Third-party code in init.txt
============================

The Lua section of init.txt (everything from the "BRC" banner down) is generated from BRC ("Buehler RC"),
https://github.com/brianfaires/crawl-rc, which is distributed under the MIT license below. The included
modules are: core (constants, util, text, mpr, item, you, equipment, options, data, config, hotkey, brc)
and the features alert-monsters, fully-recover, go-up-macro, inscribe-stats, misc-alerts,
quiver-reminders and safe-stairs.

Changes made to the upstream source: a single line in the hotkey module is guarded
(`if f_pickup_alert then f_pickup_alert.pause_alerts() end`) because the pickup-alert feature is not
included; the BRC config is set to the "Custom" config with emojis off and the low-HP alert at 35%.
Everything else is unmodified.

